  "ingredients": [
    "7 cups water, divided",
    "3 cups long grain white rice",
    "0.75 cup butter",
    "1 large onion, chopped",
    "1 clove garlic, chopped",
    "0.25 cup all-purpose flour",
    "2 tablespoons canned tomato sauce",
    "1 pound crawfish tails",
    "6 green onions, chopped",
    "1.5 tablespoons Cajun seasoning, or to taste",
    "salt and pepper to taste"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/gkhjpaDeyD3lzXXcMkudAFKgI_Y=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-76155-louisiana-crawfish-etouffee-DDMFS-4x3-step-01-df1bedcaad0c4f588304853b78dddd79.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/76155/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine 6 cups water and rice in a saucepan; bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to low, cover the pan, and simmer until rice is tender and water has been absorbed, 15 to 20 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/q8HeX_xQgsB4fvb-GG6jD4ylb50=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-76155-louisiana-crawfish-etouffee-DDMFS-4x3-step-02-1c20fbfc52cc41f5acd15e2c3862d3b4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/76155/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, melt butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onion; cook and stir until translucent. Stir in garlic; cook until fragrant, about 1 minute.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GET6IP0Go4if1G7-wDxi6xurHiA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-76155-louisiana-crawfish-etouffee-DDMFS-4x3-step-03-6b6051c4d0054143b4cfae16c7fcd076.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/76155/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in flour until blended; gradually stir in tomato sauce and remaining 1 cup water. Add crawfish tails; bring to a simmer.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ptMm90tdl-NeH54oC4eXsTiGAI0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-76155-louisiana-crawfish-etouffee-DDMFS-4x3-step-04-d96577b1e36d4f61ad49cba9da08df78.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/76155/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in green onions; season with Cajun seasoning, salt, and black pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GrXxEH_Y5iLmUSsKWEkLKgYsiX4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-76155-louisiana-crawfish-etouffee-DDMFS-4x3-step-05-9d5f063f006e4ee590c5a8debae2141d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/76155/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduce heat to low; simmer until crawfish is cooked through but not tough, 5 to 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/mWVtajm-OPjWEPHE32RtSSFXY9Q=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-76155-louisiana-crawfish-etouffee-DDMFS-4x3-step-07-9e53a5f0bb454264ababfc91f83e4c99.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/76155/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve étouffée over cooked rice.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GQWS2rm7LUGPgcHzamZOF9l2fyU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-76155-louisiana-crawfish-etouffee-DDMFS-4x3-72a6cc63adfb42a497ae1a1b355ad491.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/76155/step_07.webp"
